# Redmine's Mercurial adapter assembled the hg command line from
# request-derived values passed as standalone arguments next to their option
# flags (CWE-88, argument injection). Mercurial's early option parser rescans
# the whole command line for its own global options -- --config, --repo,
# --debugger -- even where a subcommand has begun, so a standalone
# --config=alias.rhdiff=!xterm anywhere in the argv turns one hg invocation
# into arbitrary command execution. The values arrive from the repository
# browser routes (path, identifier, branch, limit) and reach hg as their own
# argv elements, after per-element shell quoting that escapes shell
# metacharacters but leaves a leading -- intact.
#
# Ticket #27516 landed as three commits in the same minute: 58ed8655 inserts
# the end-of-options separator before the positional paths, ca87bf76 (the pool
# row) adds a blocklist over hg's early-parsing flags inside hg(), and
# 9d797400 glues each value into its flag ("-r#{value}", "--limit=#{value}")
# so no value can stand alone and be rescanned as an option. The pool row's
# parent is the fully-vulnerable tree and the remediation is present at the
# commit; no pool correction.
#
# Nothing reports either revision, re-measured over three --cache off runs per
# revision: 877 findings on the full tree at the parent and 877 at the fix,
# and no finding in lib/redmine/scm/adapters/*.rb at either revision.
#
# The argument-injection vocabulary that was missing here has since shipped.
# code.CommandOptionInjection is consumed by VYQL-INJ-031 and VYQL-VAL-004,
# code.CommandOptionInjectionSink by VYQL-INJ-280, and Ruby emitters exist for
# both (bindings/ruby/dragonfly_convert_step_raw_arguments.vyql,
# bindings/ruby/git_argv_positional_value.vyql). All three rules report zero
# tree-wide here. The two Ruby emitters are library-shaped -- Dragonfly's
# process!/generate! job steps and ruby-git's Git::Lib command runner, keyed
# on their documented parameter names -- and neither matches an application's
# own private runner.
#
# The one token-level discriminator the Ruby frontend already exposes for
# this shape, the expr: token over the append chain, does not separate the
# revisions. A probe binding over containsAny(node.context.expr, ["<<'--",
# "<<'-", "<<\"--", "<<\"-"]) with a process-runner call witness reported 42
# findings on this tree: 8 in mercurial_adapter.rb and 34 across the other
# four SCM adapters (cvs, bazaar, git, subversion), which build their command
# vectors the same way -- and the identical four functions in
# mercurial_adapter.rb (each_revision, nodes_in_branch, diff and hg itself)
# at the fixed revision, because the fix keeps
# full_args << '--config' << "extensions.redminehelper=#{HG_HELPER_EXT}"
# for ancient-Mercurial compatibility and the '--' separator appends.
# Appending a quoted flag as its own element is how every adapter in this
# project assembles a command, so it is a project idiom rather than a defect
# signal, and a binding over it reports the same count before and after the
# fix.
#
# The command-injection fallback stays closed for two reasons that both still
# hold. hg(*args, &block) lowers to a call the solver reports UNRESOLVED (no
# callee body), so taint terminates at the adapter boundary; and
# processArgVectorApplicator (internal/bindings/bindings_apply.go, registered
# for ruby only) stamps core.ProcessArgVector -- which refines
# core.ShellEscape and neutralizes injection.CommandInjection -- on every
# code.Seq whose first element is not Name/Call/Format/Index/Seq/Lambda, with
# no check that the sequence reaches a process as an argv vector.
# Re-measured minimal pair with a params[:rev] source:
# ['rhcat','-r',rev,'--','/x'].join(' ') into IO.popen reports 0 with the
# stamp, and 1 CRITICAL VYQL-INJ-002 when the first element is a variable.
# Neither is the half worth fixing here anyway: the remediation leaves the
# params -> IO.popen path intact, and the per-element shell_quote means the
# honest class of this weakness is CWE-88 rather than CWE-78, so a
# command-injection finding reports identically at both revisions.
#
# What separates the revisions is the lexical adjacency of flag and value
# inside one argv element, and the Ruby frontend emits no call-argument
# tokens: rbStructuredContextTokens
# (internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/ruby.go) emits assign, expr, field,
# call_path, call, selector, index, index_base, index_key, literal,
# interpolation and regex tokens only. A call whose argument list mixes
# option-flag literals with values -- hg 'rhcat', '-r', rev, '--', path --
# therefore cannot be told from the glued form at the binding layer, and
# keying on hg, hg_args or shellout would encode this project's own names.
# Both cases reject VYQL-INJ-031; when the Ruby frontend emits call-argument
# tokens and an argv-adjacency binding reaches this shape, the standalone
# form must flip to expect.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-analysis-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1664: a request-derived revision reaches hg as a standalone argument after its flag"
  lang ruby
  file lib/redmine/scm/adapters/mercurial_adapter.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-031
  code
  ```
  module Redmine
    module Scm
      module Adapters
        class MercurialAdapter
          def cat(path, identifier = nil)
            rev = params[:rev]
            hg 'rhcat', '-r', rev, '--', path do |io|
              io.binmode
              io.read
            end
          end

          def hg(*args, &block)
            full_args = ['-R', root_url, '--encoding', 'utf-8']
            full_args += args
            shellout(
              self.class.sq_bin + ' ' + full_args.map { |e| shell_quote e.to_s }.join(' '),
              &block
            )
          end

          def shellout(cmd, &block)
            IO.popen(cmd, 'r+') { |io| block.call(io) }
          end

          def root_url
            '/var/repos/project'
          end

          def params
            {}
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1664: the fixed revision glues the value into the flag's own argument"
  lang ruby
  file lib/redmine/scm/adapters/mercurial_adapter.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-031
  code
  ```
  module Redmine
    module Scm
      module Adapters
        class MercurialAdapter
          def cat(path, identifier = nil)
            rev = params[:rev]
            hg 'rhcat', "-r#{rev}", '--', path do |io|
              io.binmode
              io.read
            end
          end

          def hg(*args, &block)
            full_args = ["-R#{root_url}", '--encoding=utf-8']
            full_args += args
            shellout(
              self.class.sq_bin + ' ' + full_args.map { |e| shell_quote e.to_s }.join(' '),
              &block
            )
          end

          def shellout(cmd, &block)
            IO.popen(cmd, 'r+') { |io| block.call(io) }
          end

          def root_url
            '/var/repos/project'
          end

          def params
            {}
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```
